{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01024",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.38,
      "end_seconds": 2.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Welcome. Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.71,
      "end_seconds": 6.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 8.76,
      "end_seconds": 13.93,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "hello, doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.73,
      "end_seconds": 23.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here. Is this your first time with this clinic?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.17,
      "end_seconds": 29.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Mm, first time with this one, yes. A friend recommended it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.97,
      "end_seconds": 32.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "What's the main thing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.9,
      "end_seconds": 41.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Mainly gritty tired eyes. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.58,
      "end_seconds": 44.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.86,
      "end_seconds": 51.82,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Around about four days... no wait, it's more like ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.41,
      "end_seconds": 62.85,
      "duration_seconds": 10.44,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.82,
      "end_seconds": 80.75,
      "duration_seconds": 16.93,
      "text": "Maybe a five out of ten on a bad day. Only blinking breaks, and it's not much. And, And there's blurry vision that clears when I blink as well, two days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.3,
      "end_seconds": 85.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.43,
      "end_seconds": 94.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "It's a... um, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.85,
      "end_seconds": 102.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.73,
      "end_seconds": 121.94,
      "duration_seconds": 18.21,
      "text": "Hmm, for the anxiety, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. I'm on Foracort inhaler, twice a day for my asthma. I'm on artificial tears, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.96,
      "end_seconds": 127.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.96,
      "end_seconds": 135.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.78,
      "end_seconds": 139.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.32,
      "end_seconds": 144.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.01,
      "end_seconds": 147.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.31,
      "end_seconds": 157.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "I think I reacted to to some antibiotic once, years ago i don't remember which one, or what happened exactly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.36,
      "end_seconds": 163.49,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Okay, what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.17,
      "end_seconds": 170.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid. My aunt has rheumatoid arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.64,
      "end_seconds": 175.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.02,
      "end_seconds": 187.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Yes, diabetes. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.08,
      "end_seconds": 189.78,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.53,
      "end_seconds": 193.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "I've had anxiety, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.82,
      "end_seconds": 195.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "hm, okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.45,
      "end_seconds": 200.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "I have asthma, for nearly five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.96,
      "end_seconds": 207.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Right, right. Have you had any loss of vision or sensitivity to light?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.72,
      "end_seconds": 224.53,
      "duration_seconds": 14.81,
      "text": "No, no loss of vision, no sensitivity to light. I did have redness by the evening at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.38,
      "end_seconds": 229.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "And what about discharge, double vision or eye pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.93,
      "end_seconds": 233.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.8,
      "end_seconds": 238.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.13,
      "end_seconds": 245.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, uh, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 262.41,
      "end_seconds": 275.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.6,
      "text": "doctor, I've got the readings for you respiratory rate 16, BP is 126 over 74, pulse 80. Temp 36.7 degrees, SpO2 97 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.45,
      "end_seconds": 277.15,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.48,
      "end_seconds": 282.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.68,
      "end_seconds": 295.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.6,
      "end_seconds": 299.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.83,
      "end_seconds": 322.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "the eyes look a little pink but the corneas are clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.96,
      "end_seconds": 347.31,
      "duration_seconds": 20.35,
      "text": "so, you can relax now from what you've told me and what I found, this looks most like dry eye. Digital eye strain is still possible stop me if I've got anything wrong you've had gritty tired eyes for ten days, and no loss of vision or double vision"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.1,
      "end_seconds": 350.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.8,
      "end_seconds": 376.44,
      "duration_seconds": 21.64,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an eye check for gritty eyes. Look away from the screen every twenty minutes and blink fully. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Let's review you in four weeks. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.42,
      "end_seconds": 381.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.55,
      "end_seconds": 383.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}